user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 26,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_acknowledges_op_premise_before_diverging",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments) judged against the OP title/argument: 1 if any comment explicitly acknowledges validity of the OP's premise and then introduces disagreement or divergence within that same comment.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument and OC_comments jointly. OC_comments is a JSON list of comments by users other than the OP; order is not chronology. Identify the OP's main/initial premise from title and argument (argument may contain later edits; do not infer an initial snapshot, use the premise as stated). Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly states that the OP's premise (or a clearly identified core premise of the OP's view) is valid, correct, reasonable or true (e.g. 'you're right that...', 'your historical analysis is not wrong'), and THEN, in the same comment, introduces a point of divergence, disagreement or counter-claim. Acknowledgement must be explicit and about the OP's premise, not mere politeness, thanks, or restating the OP's view, and not acknowledgement of a side point. Quoted text from others and moderator/bot notices do not count. Return 0 if the comments are parsed and no comment does this. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable, or title/argument are missing; an empty comment list gives 0 only if the list parses as empty."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 49,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_acknowledges_valid_point_before_disagreeing",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: explicitly acknowledges a valid point underlying the OP's view, then afterwards introduces a discrepancy/objection (1) or not (0).",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (for OP view context) and the OC_comments JSON list (comments by other users; list order is not chronology). Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly states that some underlying point, concern or part of the OP's view is valid/correct/reasonable (e.g. 'you're right that...', 'fair point') AND, later within that same comment, introduces a disagreement, counterexample or discrepancy. The acknowledgment must be about the OP's position, not merely about a side fact, politeness, or empathy, and must precede the objection. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none do this (including pure refutations or agreement-only comments). Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable or empty. Do not use conversation or later replies; ignore quoted text from others unless the commenter adopts it."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 60,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_concedes_op_component_before_counterexample",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment (OC_comments): explicitly acknowledges validity of a specific component of the OP's argument and then presents a counter-example; 1 if any comment does so.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument (OP context) and the OC_comments JSON list (comments by other users; order is not chronology). Return 1 if at least one comment, in its own voice, (a) explicitly acknowledges that a specific identifiable component of the OP's view/argument (a particular claim, premise or point, not generic politeness like 'good post' or a blanket 'you have a point') is valid/correct/reasonable, and (b) subsequently within the same comment presents a counter-example (a specific case, instance or scenario that contradicts or limits the OP's claim). Acknowledgment must come before the counter-example in the comment text. Exclude quoted text from others, reported positions not adopted by the commenter, and bot/moderator notices. Return 0 if the comments are assessable and no comment meets both conditions. Return null if OC_comments is missing/unparseable or title/argument is missing; an empty list gives 0. Do not use any outcome or view-change information."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
